# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# rb's own scratch: caches and runtime environments it creates under the repo
# root so nothing has to be writable outside the checkout.
.rb/

# Zephyr/CMake build trees, one per target+workload+mode.
build/

# mill build output for hardware/ospi
hardware/ospi/out/

# Published separately; see tools/collect-bitstreams.py
bitstreams/
dts/
elfs/

# Verilator build output for hardware/pwm
hardware/pwm/obj_dir/

# Per-run camera captures. hardware/ospi/bootup-capture.gdb dumps the frame and
# its PNG into whatever directory rb debug was invoked from, which is normally
# the repo root -- so following the camera docs otherwise leaves the tree dirty
# every single run. The keepable frames live in docs/figures/.
bootup-frame.raw
bootup-frame.png
bootup-frame-colour.png

# Vivado outputs for the bare-metal pad tests. The Verilog, XDC, TCL and the
# build/verify logs ARE tracked -- they are the evidence that F13's output
# driver is dead -- but the 9.9 MB bitstreams and checkpoints are not.
hardware/padtest/out/
hardware/padtest/*/out/

# Per-session telemetry CSVs from tools/bench/riskybird-dash.py, which defaults
# to ./riskybird-logs -- i.e. the repo root, since that is where the bring-up
# guide runs it from. Same reasoning as the camera captures above: a tool you run
# every bench session must not dirty the tree every bench session.
riskybird-logs/
